%N A072461 Numbers k such that sigma(k) == 1 (mod 4).
%C A072461 All the terms are squares or twice squares. k = 2^e * m^2, where m is odd, is a term if and only if the number of primes p == 1 (mod 4) with odd valuation v_p(m) is even for e = 0, and odd for e > 0. - _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 02 2026
%H A072461 Ray Chandler, <a href="/A072461/b072461.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a> (first 1000 terms from Harvey P. Dale)
%F A072461 Sum_{n>=1} 1/a(n) = Pi^2/8 (A111003). - _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 02 2026
%t A072461 Select[Range[5000],Mod[DivisorSigma[1,#],4]==1&] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Oct 24 2016 *)
%o A072461 (PARI) isok(n) = ((sigma(n) % 4) == 1);
